Cycle 3 — tools/exp06_finalize.py (plan §5/§6.4 completion-by-run-type). CLI: `python tools/exp06_finalize.py --run-dir <dir> --run-type {full,smoke,probe,haa_train,haa_eval,haa_job} --log <path> --child-exit <int> [--repo <path>]`. Reads the run dir, verifies per run type and writes `completion.json` via provenance.write_completion (refusing to overwrite an existing completion unless byte-identical): FULL — provenance.json present and its source-closure digest equals a fresh closure_record of the same file list at the same commit (drift → refuse), args.json passes exp06_recipe.check_all, history.jsonl passes check_budget, last.pth has epoch 12 / batch_idx 0 and its `args` pass the schema, `epoch_012.pth` state_dict equals last.pth['model'] tensor-wise (torch.equal per key, same key set), child_exit == 0, the log file exists and its last line is `EXP06_CHILD_EXIT <code> <iso-time>` with the same code (the launcher appends it; this is the "closed log" evidence), sha256 of epoch_012.pth/last.pth/history.jsonl/args.json/provenance.json/log recorded, `run_type: full`; SMOKE/PROBE — no artifacts required, `diagnostic: true`, records the smoke receipt path/hash if given (`--receipt`), never admissible as an arm (`admissible_arm: false`); HAA_TRAIN — args.json (with heading/frame/init_sha256 keys present when frame == heading), history.jsonl, summary.json, best.pth, last.pth hashes, child_exit 0, log marker; HAA_EVAL — args.json, metrics_<room>.json, per_sample_<room>.json hashes for the single room named in args, meta.heading present when frame == heading, child_exit 0, log marker; HAA_JOB — `--children <dir>...`: every child dir has a completion.json, their hashes recorded, the expected set (stage1 + 4 stage2 + 4 eval, or 4 eval for zeroshot) enforced via `--expect {finetune,zeroshot}`. All failures are ValueError with a named cause; exit 2; nothing written on failure. Tests with synthetic directories and tiny tensors: full success path; each refusal (truncated budget, state-dict mismatch, missing epoch_012, non-zero exit, missing/incorrect log marker, closure drift via a modified file copy in a temp repo clone, existing different completion); haa_train/haa_eval/haa_job success and refusal cases; idempotent re-run yields identical completion bytes.

Cycle 4 — tools/exp06_smoke.py (plan §9 rung 4, R3.3). `--entry {trainer,exp06_train,exp06_haa_finetune,exp06_haa_eval} [--receipt <path>] [--alarm-seconds 300] [--max-gb 3] -- <argv...>`: imports the entry module (trainer = train_xRIR_backbone with sys.argv patched for its argv-less main; the others call `main(argv)`), runs it in-process under `signal.alarm`, measures wall time and `torch.cuda.max_memory_allocated()` (0 when CUDA is unavailable), aborts (SystemExit 3) if the alarm fires or the peak exceeds --max-gb after the run, prints one JSON line `EXP06_SMOKE {...}` and writes the receipt (`diagnostic: true`, entry, argv, wall_s, peak_bytes, exit_status, git_head, timestamp). `--make-fixture <path> [--seed 0]`: CPU-constructs `build_xrir_exp06('cylindrical_oriented', 8)` with torch.manual_seed(seed) and saves its state_dict (plus a sidecar `<path>.json` with sha256 and the registry digest). The HAA entries do not exist yet (round 2b): dispatch by module name string and test with a stub module injected into sys.modules. Tests: alarm abort path (stub entry that sleeps), max-gb refusal (monkeypatch max_memory_allocated), receipt fields, fixture loads strictly into build_xrir_exp06('cylindrical_oriented', 8), unknown entry refused.

Cycle 5 — tools/exp06_launch.sh: `tools/exp06_launch.sh <smoke|probe|full|finalize> --gpu <g> --reviewed-commit <sha> [--attempt-root ckpt/exp06/pretrain/xRIR_cylor_8_shot] [--dry-run]`. Preflight (a small Python helper inside tools/exp06_finalize.py, subcommand `preflight`): HEAD == reviewed commit, tree clean outside worklog/ (provenance.checked_git_state), no other exp06 launch pid alive, for `full`/`probe` GPU <g> has no compute apps (nvidia-smi --query-compute-apps=pid --format=csv,noheader -i <g>) — refuse otherwise. `full`: creates `<attempt-root>/attempt_<UTC>` exclusively, runs `python tools/exp06_train.py --backbone cylindrical_oriented --save-dir <attempt> --num-shot 8 --max-len 9600 --lr 1e-3 --weight-decay 1e-4 --decay-epochs 3 --lr-gamma 0.1 --epochs 12 --batch-size 32 --accum-steps 2 --num-workers 12 --seed 0 --tf32 --log-interval 50 --save-every 500 --epoch-ckpt-every 1 --run-type full` under `nohup setsid` with `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=<g> PYTHONHASHSEED=0 OMP_NUM_THREADS=8`, tees stdout/stderr to `worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_06_oriented_cyl_claude/oriented_cyl_<ts>_train_full.log`, writes `<attempt>/launch.pid`, waits, appends `EXP06_CHILD_EXIT <code> <iso>` to the log, then runs the finalizer (`--run-type full`); on non-zero exit renames the attempt `attempt_<UTC>_ABORTED_<reason>`; on success creates/updates the promotion symlink `<attempt-root>/final -> attempt_<UTC>`. `probe`: same via `tools/exp06_smoke.py --entry exp06_train` with `--epochs 1 --max-train-batches 200 --max-test-batches 20 --no-save --run-type probe --batch-size 32 --accum-steps 2 --tf32 --num-workers 12` and receipt `<attempt-root>/probe_<UTC>.json`; `smoke`: the §9 (a)/(b) commands via the smoke runner on the given GPU. `--dry-run` prints every command and path without executing. Tests (tests/test_exp06_smoke.py or a new tests/test_exp06_launch.py): `bash -n`; dry-run golden output for the three modes (argv exactly as plan §5/§9); preflight refusals via the Python helper (dirty tree in a temp clone, wrong HEAD, pid alive, GPU busy via a fake nvidia-smi on PATH).

After each cycle run the touched tests; at the end `python -m py_compile` on new .py files, `bash -n tools/exp06_launch.sh`, `git diff --check`, and `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' python -m pytest tests/test_exp06_*.py tests/test_provenance.py -q -p no:cacheprovider`. Finish by printing commit SHAs, per-commit line counts, test counts, and every spec/code discrepancy (do not deviate silently).
